subject: fix(cli): conditional log for tray runtime self-heal failure (GAP-P3-01)

Move ensureTrayRuntime self-heal from top-of-file (before arg parsing) to
after --tray/-t flag and the auto-relaunch tray fallback are resolved.

The previous location had a temporal-dead-zone hazard: referencing
`trayMode` at line 89 (its declaration is line 124) would throw a
ReferenceError, which is strictly worse than the empty catch it aimed to
replace. Moving the call to after the auto-relaunch fallback also means
the fallback path (skipUpdate + no TTY → trayMode=true) is correctly
covered.

Behavior:
- Install remains unconditional so systray2 is pre-cached for future
  --tray invocations (preserving original pre-install intent).
- On failure AND tray was requested: log '[tray-runtime] install failed:
  <msg>' plus a two-line diagnostic explaining the headless fallback.
- On failure AND tray was NOT requested: silent (no noise on every
  non-tray startup).
- Server continues in headless mode on failure — no crash.

Verified:
- node --check cli/cli.js → SYNTAX OK
- TEST 1: --tray + stub throwing ensureTrayRuntime → emits full diagnostic
- TEST 2: no --tray + same stub → completely silent (correct)

Fixes GAP-P3-01 from comprehensive gap analysis.

